gcm/live-draw: Killzone 2's SPU post chain: local-memory surface write-back, SPU puts into local memory uploaded at bind/present, command-word watch.

Symptom: the scene is drawn into a LOCAL-memory target (0x7B0000 v1.01, 0x760000 1.29) whose
EA the PPU hands to the SPU post-processing chain (WWS Gfx.Post.* jobs), and the last draw of each frame samples the
other display buffer, which only the SPU chain writes. Patch 2017 wrote back main-memory surfaces only, and the SPU
write hook (KZ3 2033) only marked pages for texture hashing; the 2017 band hash can miss an SPU write that lands before
the walker's flip baseline.

Fix:
- rsx_live_draw_before_guest_sync also writes back local colour surfaces chosen by LD_LOCAL_WRITEBACK (0/unset off;
  1|auto = GPU-written local colour surfaces that are not display buffers and have >= LD_LOCAL_WB_MIN_PIXELS pixels,
  default 640*360; `post` = as auto once rsx_live_draw_local_writeback_arm() was called, which the KZ2 port does when
  the game's post stage renders; or a comma list of hex offsets). LD_WB_LOG=N logs each local write-back with a non-black count.
- SPU puts into local memory (cellGcm_note_guest_write_pages_ea, the SPU hook's only user) set bits in a separate
  page bitmap; ld_gv_validate (texture bind, write-back) and the present consume the bits under a surface and upload
  those rows from guest memory. LD_SPU_LOCAL_UPLOAD=0 disables, LD_SPU_LOCAL_LOG=N logs marks and applies.
- LD_FAKE_POST=1 (test aid): after a local write-back, copy that surface's guest rows into every local display buffer
  and report it through the SPU hook, standing in for the post chain.
- cellGcm_watch_cmd_ea(ea, tag): the walker logs the word it finds at up to 8 watched command addresses each time
  it changes (GCM_CMD_WATCH_LOG=N, default 64); the port registers the post stage's command-stream patch word P.

Verification: Killzone 2 under Proton.
Rebased 2026-10-19 onto KZ3 2044-2086 (context of the SPU hook moved by 2078/2080).

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0: context and offsets only.

